The City Council, in order to promote the public health, safety, and general welfare of
the citizens and landowners of the City of Norfolk, and accomplish the objectives of
the Code of Virginia and City Charter, and implement the city’s comprehensive plan
and other adopted plans and planning documents, adopts this Ordinance with the
following purpose and intent, where applicable:

A. To provide for adequate light, air, convenience of access, and safety from fire,
flood, structure failure, crime, and other dangers;

B. To reduce or prevent congestion in the public streets;
C. To facilitate the creation of a convenient, attractive, and harmonious community;
D. To facilitate the provision of adequate police and fire protection, disaster
evacuation, civil defense, transportation, water, sewerage, flood protection,

